Privacy Policy
for PrepList (the “App”)
Effective Date: [Effective Date] | Last Updated: [Last Updated Date]
This Privacy Policy explains how [Company / Developer Legal Name] (“we,” “us,” or “our”) collects, uses,
stores, and protects information when you use the PrepList mobile and web application (the “App”),
available on Android and iOS and built using Google Firebase. PrepList is a kitchen prep-management tool
that helps restaurant staff create, assign, and track daily prep tasks by kitchen section (e.g. Grill, Pastry,
Prep, Sauce, Cold Section).
By creating an account or otherwise using the App, you agree to the collection and use of information in
accordance with this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with the terms of this policy, please do not use the
App.
1. Information We Collect
1.1 Information You Provide Directly
When staff create an account or use the App, we may collect:
• Account information: name, email address, and password (or PIN, if PIN-based login is enabled).
• Profile information: job role (e.g. Chef, Line Cook, Pastry) and assigned kitchen section(s).
• Task content: prep task names, descriptions, notes, and status updates (Pending, In Progress,
Completed) that you or other staff create.
• Photos: images you voluntarily attach to a completed task (captured with the device camera or
chosen from the photo library) to verify quality and completion.
1.2 Information Collected Automatically
As you use the App, certain information may be collected automatically:
• Activity & usage data: which tasks were created, updated, or completed; timestamps of these
actions; and the activity feed shown to your team (e.g. “John completed Chicken Stock – 2:15 PM”).
• Login & session data: sign-in timestamps and which staff members are currently active in the App,
used to power the real-time staff-visibility dashboard.
• Device & technical data: device type, operating system version, unique device/installation
identifiers, app version, and crash/diagnostic logs, collected to keep the App stable and secure.
1.3 Information We Do Not Intentionally Collect
We do not knowingly collect precise geolocation, contacts, biometric data, or payment card details directly
within the App. If a paid subscription is purchased, payment is handled by the applicable app store (Google
Play / Apple App Store) or a third-party payment processor, and we do not receive or store your full
payment card information.
2. How We Use Your Information
We use the information described above to:
• Create and manage staff accounts and authenticate logins.
• Operate core App features, including section-based prep lists, task assignment, and status tracking.
• Show which staff are currently active and what they are working on, in real time.
• Record who created, updated, or completed a task, and attach the relevant date, time, and optional
photo, for accountability and quality control.
• Generate the daily and weekly history/reporting views used by chefs and managers.
• Provide reusable prep templates linked to a section.
• Maintain, secure, troubleshoot, and improve the App.
• Communicate with restaurant administrators about their account, subscription, or service updates.
• Process subscription/billing status for the Premium tier (multi-location support, advanced reports,
staff analytics), where applicable.
We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use kitchen task data or staff photos for
advertising purposes.
3. Firebase and Third-Party Services
PrepList is built on Google Firebase. We use the following Firebase services, provided by Google LLC, to
operate the App:
• Firebase Authentication: to create and manage staff logins securely.
• Cloud Firestore: to store and sync prep tasks, sections, staff assignments, and activity/history data
in real time.
• Firebase Storage: to store photos attached to completed tasks.
• Cloud Functions: to run backend logic such as processing task updates, notifications, and
subscription/monetization checks.
These providers may process data on servers located outside your country. Google's use of this data is
governed by the Firebase Privacy and Security policy and Google's own privacy policy. We do not share
your data with third parties for their own marketing purposes.
Restaurant owners/administrators may also connect the App to [any additional third-party service, e.g.
payment processor / analytics provider] to enable optional features; if so, that provider's own privacy
policy will also apply.
4. Data Storage and Security
All account, task, and photo data is stored on Google's Firebase cloud infrastructure, which applies
industry-standard security measures, including encryption in transit and at rest, and access controls
restricted by staff role and assigned section.
We take reasonable technical and organizational steps to protect your information from unauthorized
access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. However, no method of electronic transmission or storage is
100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
Only staff members with an active account for a given restaurant, and their chef/manager, can access that
restaurant's task data and photos. [Describe any additional admin/owner access controls, if
applicable.]
5. Data Retention
• Daily task history is retained to allow end-of-day review by chefs and managers.
• Weekly history is retained for at least the last 7 days, and may be retained longer ([specify
retention period, e.g. 12 months]) to support trend and performance reviews.
• Photos attached to completed tasks are retained for as long as the associated task record is
retained, after which they are deleted.
• Account information is retained for as long as the account is active, and for [specify period, e.g.
30/90 days] after account deletion to allow for recovery, unless a longer period is required by law.
You or your restaurant administrator may request deletion of your account and associated personal data
