6. Your Rights and Choices
Depending on your location, you may have the right to:
• Access the personal information we hold about you.
• Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete information.
• Request deletion of your personal information, subject to the limitations described in Section 5.
• Withdraw consent to photo capture where the App offers this as an optional feature.
• Object to or request restriction of certain processing of your information.
To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at [support/contact email]. Because PrepList is
typically deployed by a restaurant as the account administrator, some requests (e.g. account creation or
deactivation) may need to be handled by your employer/restaurant administrator.
7. Camera and Photo Library Permission
The App requests access to your device's camera and/or photo library only to let you attach an optional
photo when marking a prep task as completed. This permission is optional, is requested at the time of use,
and can be managed at any time from your device's settings. If permission is denied or revoked, you can
still use the App and mark tasks as completed without attaching a photo.
8. Children's Privacy
PrepList is a workplace tool intended for use by restaurant staff and is not directed to, and should not be
used by, individuals under the age of 16 (or the applicable minimum working age in your jurisdiction, if
higher). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If we become aware that we have
inadvertently collected such information, we will take steps to delete it promptly. Contact us at
[support/contact email] if you believe a minor has provided us with personal information.
9. International Data Transfers
Because the App uses Google Firebase, your information may be transferred to, stored, and processed in
countries other than the one in which you or your restaurant are located, including [e.g. the United
States]. Where required by applicable law, we rely on appropriate safeguards (such as Google's standard
contractual clauses) to protect information transferred internationally.
10. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes to the App, our practices, or legal
requirements. When we make material changes, we will update the “Last Updated” date at the top of this
policy and, where appropriate, notify restaurant administrators through the App or by email. Continued use
of the App after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
